# THE SPATIAL LATENT UPSCALER PIN.
#
# ONE LINE, "<huggingface-repo> <revision-sha>", turns multi-scale generation
# on. Blank and the media image is built exactly as it is today: ltxcaps
# reports latent_upsampler_baked=false, videogen records
# upscaler_absent_reason=latent-upsampler-not-baked on every clip, and the
# single-scale path runs unchanged.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHAT IS ALREADY VERIFIED — fetched 2026-08-31, not recalled
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# REPOSITORY   a-r-r-o-w/LTX-0.9.8-Latent-Upsampler
#              Named by the official diffusers LTX documentation
#              (huggingface/diffusers @ main,
#              docs/source/en/api/pipelines/ltx_video.md, line 342) as the
#              0.9.8 latent upsampler, loaded via
#              LTXLatentUpsamplerModel.from_pretrained and paired with
#              LTXLatentUpsamplePipeline(vae=pipeline.vae, latent_upsampler=…).
#              That is exactly how videogen._load_real_upsampler builds it.
#
#              Upstream's own comment on that line reads
#              "TODO: Update the checkpoint here once updated in LTX org",
#              so this is a staging location the docs point at rather than a
#              Lightricks-org repository. That is a reason to pin a revision,
#              not a reason to avoid the model — but it is why the revision
#              matters more here than usual, and it belongs in the record.
#
# MODEL CLASS  LTXLatentUpsamplerModel, dims=3, in_channels=128,
#              mid_channels=512, num_blocks_per_stage=4,
#              spatial_upsample=true, temporal_upsample=false.
#              The Dockerfile asserts every one of those fields and refuses a
#              config that differs — a temporal or 2-D variant would construct
#              happily and then hand the refine pass latents it cannot use.
#
# SIZE         126.25 M parameters, computed from the architecture in
#              diffusers 0.38.0 (pipelines/ltx/modeling_latent_upsampler.py).
#              At fp32 that is 505.0 MB — matching the published artifact size
#              to the megabyte, which independently confirms dims=3.
#              About 1.2% of the ~40 GiB media image. Disk is not the blocker.
#
# COMPATIBILITY  LTXLatentUpsamplePipeline takes exactly two modules, `vae` and
#              `latent_upsampler`, so it reuses the VAE already baked and adds
#              no other weights. Verified by reading the installed
#              diffusers==0.38.0 source, not the documentation.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHAT IS NOT VERIFIED, AND CANNOT BE FROM THE BUILD CONTAINER
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# THE REVISION SHA and THE LICENCE TEXT.
#
# huggingface.co is refused by this environment's egress proxy (403 to
# CONNECT, confirmed again 2026-08-31 for huggingface.co, hf.co and
# cdn-lfs.huggingface.co). A revision sha and a repository's licence file are
# registry metadata and exist nowhere else, so neither can be read from here.
#
# Writing a plausible-looking sha would be a fabrication wearing the costume
# of a fact, and a revision IS the licence: the LTX transformer above is
# pinned to 8984fa25007f376c1a299016d0957a37a2f797bb because the owner
# accepted the LTX Open Weights terms as they stood at those exact bytes. An
# agent cannot accept a licence on anyone's behalf.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TO ENABLE — one line, after reading the licence
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   1. Open https://huggingface.co/a-r-r-o-w/LTX-0.9.8-Latent-Upsampler
#   2. Read the licence and satisfy yourself it permits redistribution inside
#      ONIQ's private image, commercially.
#   3. Take the full commit sha from the repository's history (NOT the branch
#      name — `main` moves, and a moving pin is not a pin).
#   4. Add it below, uncommented:
#
#         a-r-r-o-w/LTX-0.9.8-Latent-Upsampler <full-40-char-sha>
#
# The build then verifies and REFUSES if any of it fails to hold: the
# revision must resolve to that exact sha, a LICENSE or NOTICE file must ship
# beside the weights, config.json must match every expected field above, the
# config must load under the installed diffusers, and the weights must be
# inside the size guard. Nothing is trusted; everything is checked where it
# can be checked.
#
# WHAT ENABLING BUYS. Measured arithmetic: the generation canvas is 704 wide
# and the delivered film is 1080, so assembly resamples every frame UP by
# 1.534x today, and a pixel resampler cannot invent detail that was never
# sampled. With the upscaler present the clip is generated at 704x1248,
# upsampled 2x IN LATENT SPACE, partially re-denoised at 1408x2496 so the
# transformer actually synthesises the detail, and only then decoded — and the
# film's 1080 becomes a DOWNSCALE of real detail. GPU time is unmeasured; the
# refine pass is real additional inference at 4x the pixels and no cost claim
# should be made about it before a real generation.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RESOLVED 2026-08-31 — measured from the registry, not transcribed
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# gpu-validation.yml mode `upscaler-discover` read both candidates the diffusers
# documentation names, with the runner's HF_TOKEN, and measured:
#
#   Lightricks/ltxv-spatial-upscaler-0.9.7
#     revision   c96c168c2bd8bbc82c9fe8259e5f89f8b2ea293f
#     licence    ships LTX-Video-Open-Weights-License-0.X.txt
#     shape      diffusers PIPELINE — latent_upsampler/, media/, vae/
#     component  latent_upsampler/ is 505,009,832 bytes
#     config     declares _class_name and defaults the rest
#
#   a-r-r-o-w/LTX-0.9.8-Latent-Upsampler
#     revision   e0c981533db26531c47dec16a124586cea53f11f
#     licence    NONE. Three files, no LICENSE, no NOTICE, no licence tag.
#     component  505,009,832 bytes — BYTE-IDENTICAL to the Lightricks one
#
# The two components are the same size to the byte, so they are the same
# weights: one published by Lightricks under their terms, one re-uploaded
# without any. That settles it. The third-party copy offers nothing the
# official one does not, and offers it with no licence at all, so this pin
# names the Lightricks repository.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OWNER LICENCE ACCEPTANCE — 2026-08-31
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Owner directive, 2026-08-31. The owner verified that ONIQ is below the LTX
# $10M annual-revenue threshold and therefore qualifies under the LTX-Video 0.X
# Open Weights community licence, which grants the use, reproduction and
# distribution rights ONIQ needs at no cost for entities under that threshold;
# the paid commercial licence applies at or above $10M.
#
# The acceptance is NOT a licence to ignore the conditions. The owner's words:
# "Preserve the applicable licence/attribution and use restrictions in the
# production distribution." The bake enforces the mechanical half — it refuses
# to redistribute weights whose LICENSE/NOTICE does not travel with them, and
# LTX-Video-Open-Weights-License-0.X.txt is moved down beside the component it
# licenses.
#
# An agent did not and cannot accept this on the owner's behalf; the record
# exists so the acceptance has a date and an author next to the code it governs,
# the same way the 2026-08-13 movie-on/classic-off flip does.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHAT REMAINS UNMEASURED
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This is the 0.9.7 component and ONIQ bakes the base LTX-Video (2B). The
# byte-identical size strongly suggests the "0.9.8" upsampler is the same
# artifact under a different name, so the version skew is probably cosmetic —
# but PROBABLY IS NOT MEASURED. Whether multi-scale actually improves ONIQ's
# output is unknown until a real generation is run and looked at.

Lightricks/ltxv-spatial-upscaler-0.9.7 c96c168c2bd8bbc82c9fe8259e5f89f8b2ea293f
